    "title": "<p>Classification of gestational trophoblastic diseases</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Pei Hui",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoTableGridLight\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse; border: none;\" border=\"1\" width=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 3.5pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 163.05pt; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; border-left: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; border-right: none; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"218\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Putative trophoblastic cells&nbsp;of&nbsp;origin</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.9pt; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; border-left: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; border-right: none; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"208\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Gestational trophoblastic disease classification</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 142.9pt; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; border-left: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; border-right: none; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" width=\"190\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Genetic features</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 163.05pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" rowspan=\"4\" width=\"218\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Chorionic villous trophoblasts</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 77.95pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"3\" width=\"104\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Hydatidiform mole</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 77.95pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"104\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Complete hydatidiform mole</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 142.9pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"190\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Androgenic paternal-only genome in sporadic cases; inherited mutations of <em>NLRP7<span style=\"font-style: normal;\"> (</span>NALP7</em>) or <em>KHDC3L</em> in familial biparental complete moles</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 77.95pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"104\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Partial hydatidiform mole</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 142.9pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"190\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Diandric monogynic triploidy in most cases</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 77.95pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"104\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Invasive hydatidiform mole</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 142.9pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"190\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Dependent on the prior mole</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 41.85pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.9pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 41.85pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"208\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Atypical villous lesions</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 142.9pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 41.85pt;\" width=\"190\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Unknown in most cases</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 71.45pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"6\" width=\"96\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Intermediate trophoblasts</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 91.6pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"122\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Villous intermediate trophoblasts</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.9pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"208\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Gestational choriocarcinoma</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 142.9pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"190\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Androgenetic XX genome following complete moles in most cases</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 43.75pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 91.6pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 43.75pt;\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"122\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Implantation site intermediate trophoblasts</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.9pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 43.75pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"208\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Placental site trophoblastic tumour</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 142.9pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 43.75pt;\" width=\"190\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Preferential requirement of paternal X&nbsp;chromosome</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 37.9pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.9pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 37.9pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"208\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Exaggerated implantation site reaction</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 142.9pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 37.9pt;\" width=\"190\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Unknown</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 41.15pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 91.6pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 41.15pt;\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"122\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Chorionic-type intermediate trophoblasts</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.9pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 41.15pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"208\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Epithelioid trophoblastic tumour</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 142.9pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 41.15pt;\" width=\"190\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Preferential requirement of paternal X&nbsp;chromosome</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 40.45pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.9pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 40.45pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"208\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Placental site nodule&nbsp;/ atypical placental site nodule</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 142.9pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 40.45pt;\" width=\"190\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Unknown</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 91.6pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"122\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Mixed intermediate trophoblasts</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.9pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"208\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Mixed trophoblastic tumours</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 142.9pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"190\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Unknown</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>",
